00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.521
That's our panel
that we just had.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:26.025
So, would you like to comment
on my editorial that I just did

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:29.095
about how there's a lot
of materialism in music

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:31.231
these days, and maybe
it's not great for the kids?

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.333
I think there's materialism
in American society, period.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:35.668
Your-- your-- We're just...

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.136
Musicians and artists
a lot of times,

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.804
in terms of when art
becomes commerce,

00:00:39.004 --> 00:00:40.940
is just a reflection
of where society is.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.709
When you were talking about,
you know, it used to be

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.811
a lot of bitches and hoes
and homophobia in there.

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:48.647 line:0%
Bitches, hoes
and homosexuals buy music.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.117 line:0%
At a certain point the people
who make music was like,

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.451 line:0%
"It's not cool to keep
saying this shit

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.921 line:0%
'cause they got better
buying power than just the guys

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:56.089
who are mad at home."

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.124
And what you see now
is the people on top

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.525
of the charts,
so the Kendrick Lamars,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:03.396
the Drakes, the J. Coles.
Because society... Was it...

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:07.033
Here we say it, it's not
the vanguard that moves,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.868
the people's not--
Leadership is when the people

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.369
are ready to move.
So, I think that--

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:12.238
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)
-I think...

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:13.806
(AUDIENCE APPLAUD CONTINUES)

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:17.544
...when I have arguments with
Aniyah, my 26 year old daughter,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.911
I know that
there's a change coming

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.346
because of the way
she views the world.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.681
So, I think musicians
and artists for commerce

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:23.749
are going to adjust.

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:26.052
But when it comes to money,
we have an infatuation

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:27.186
with money in this country.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.221
You know, so much to the point
we went and kidnapped

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:30.522
a bunch of people
four hundred years ago

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:33.226
and made them work for free
and say, "Boom, greatest nation
in the world."

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.360
-So, you know.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.162
-Boy, that's--
-Happy Black History Month.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.663
Happy Black History Month.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.299
It's like a relationship fight.
You never let it go.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.002
-No, you can't. (HESITATES)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.438
I'll tell you this.
Speak... speaking of money.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.139
You want to let it go. Give...

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:48.875
Prepare reparations package
for this...

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:50.643
For this. For Black people
in this country.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.744
-For people...
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.380
And... And I'll... And I'll...
And I'll tell you this.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.849
The leader of the feds
