that included

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.099
reversal of redlining
by helping Black people

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:15.902
be homeowners,
understand credit.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.639
And understand, Americans,
that if the Black community

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.907
has more money,
this country has more money.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:23.876
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUD)
-Yeah, and we need to start

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.412
seeing ourselves
in a relationship.

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:29.048
As long as we have the topic
on the table,

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.683
what don't you think
about that, reparations?

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.386
Vivek Ramaswamy just texted me
his Taylor Swift playlist,

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.520
I haven't been
paying attention to it.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.022
(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:37.823
BILL MAHER: Can't believe
you're dodging this question?

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:38.824
-I'll dodge it.
-Really?

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.193
-In terms of what? Reparations?
-Reparations.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.328
-Signing out a check.
-No. Uh, someone's gotta pay.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:45.330
No, no, I'm not for reparations.
I'm not for that at all.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.367
At the end of the day,
this country owes 34 trillion,

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.069 line:0%
and the government
doesn't owe that money.

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:52.271 line:0%
You all owe that money.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:53.606 line:0%
Don't be fooled.
Don't be fooled.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:54.841 line:0%
The money's gotta come
from somewhere.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.843
Is there a difference
between collective guilt
and individual...

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.745
-I don't want you
to feel guilty. No, I didn't--
-I don't.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.112
Because I didn't do it.

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:01.213
-I think more Black conser...
-Collective--

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.250
But you benefited from it.
You benefited from it,

00:03:04.316 --> 00:03:05.385
and you're still benefitting
from it.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.552
Yes, that's true too.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.122
So, my thing is
just help spread the benefits.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.056
But... Okay, but, you know,
there are reparations

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.391
that do go on in different ways.

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:14.093
Yeah, absolutely.
I didn't say absolutely,

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:15.762
"Just give me a few million
dollars and I'm fine."

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.564
No, I think that trade
and higher level education.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.132
I do think a cash payout.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:22.301
I think that there should be
a mortgage forgiveness.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.036
I think that
we should have an incentive

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.172
to incentivize Black wealth
in this country,

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:29.341
Robert Smith, Black billionaire,
had an interesting conversation

00:03:29.441 --> 00:03:31.244
